{"ticker": "QMCO", "quality": "strong", "sentinel": false, "analysis": "Quantum reported fiscal Q2 2027 results on Nov 9: revenue up 42.9% YoY to $89.6M (11% sequential), gross margin up 340bp YoY to 41.0%, non-GAAP net income of $9.8M ($0.25/share) and a record backlog of nearly $100M. It also announced a major hyperscale Scalar i7 Raptor order and its largest ActiveScale order. Strong revenue growth, a second straight non-GAAP profitable quarter and a record backlog make this a strong catalyst. No explicit guidance raise appears in the visible text, and the GAAP loss comes from warrant fair-value changes, so it falls short of game_changer."}
{"ticker": "HROW", "quality": "strong", "sentinel": false, "analysis": "Harrow reported record Q3 2026 revenue of $99.3M, up 41% sequentially and 39% YoY, with branded revenue up 62% YoY and Adjusted EBITDA of $21.2M. GAAP net income was inflated by a one-time $5M litigation gain, which is ignored. The revenue acceleration plus a new VEVYE coverage win is strong, but the first-half guidance miss and the lack of a confirmed guidance raise in the visible text keep this from being a game_changer. The TYRVAYA acquisition is older background, not today's catalyst."}
{"ticker": "SECZ", "quality": "routine", "sentinel": false, "analysis": "The catalyst is Q3 2026 results: revenue of $18.6M (+13% YoY), a net loss of $66.3M and record average tokenized assets of $5.0B. The release also announced a $50M buyback (about 3% of a $1.5B market cap) and the agreement to acquire River One, with no terms given. Growth is modest, there is no guidance raise, and the loss is large, so the buyback and acquisition are not material enough to count as strong. The 8-K/A only corrects a signature date and is not new news. SECZ is the buyer, so this is not an mna grade."}
{"ticker": "EIKN", "quality": "routine", "sentinel": false, "analysis": "The ~16% premarket jump appears tied to renewed attention on previously disclosed single-arm Phase 2 data for EIK1001 (72% ORR in squamous NSCLC) discussed at the Guggenheim conference. This is not a new readout, approval, or deal. A conference presentation of old data from a pre-revenue biotech is not a concrete, fresh catalyst, so it is routine."}
{"ticker": "RLGT", "quality": "strong", "sentinel": false, "analysis": "Fresh Q1 FY2027 earnings (8-K filed 2026-11-09): revenue $279.8M, up 23.4% YoY, gross profit up 16.1%, adjusted EPS $0.18 vs $0.09 (doubled), GAAP net income up 369%, and no net debt. Solid acceleration in revenue growth plus a big profit beat supports a strong grade; no explicit guidance raise is shown in the excerpt, so not game_changer. The August credit facility is background only and no deal is involved."}
{"ticker": "CSQR", "quality": "strong", "sentinel": false, "analysis": "Csquare reported Q3 2026 results: revenue up 25.6% to $302.3M, record bookings of $66.1M (14th straight quarter of sequential growth), and Adjusted EBITDA up 44.3% with margin expanding to 47.8%. No guidance figures appear in the visible text, and the net loss is driven by IPO costs, so a solid growth beat without a clear guidance raise grades as strong rather than game_changer. The fresh catalyst is the earnings release, and no deal is involved."}
{"ticker": "VMD", "quality": "routine", "sentinel": false, "analysis": "The only identifiable item is Viemed's Q3 2026 earnings (record revenue $80.7M, +12.2% YoY; EPS $0.11 vs $0.09), but it was filed on 2026-11-04, about 6 days before today's gap, so it is not a fresh catalyst. The text also shows no guidance-raise figures, and nothing new dated today explains the gap-up, so no concrete, fresh, verifiable catalyst can be identified and it is graded routine."}
{"ticker": "CCAP", "quality": "strong", "sentinel": false, "analysis": "CCAP reported Q3 2026 results: NII of $0.37/share (up from $0.36 last quarter), NAV of $17.72 (down from $17.82), and a $0.34 Q4 dividend. It also announced a new $50M buyback (~14% of its $368M market cap) plus a Sun Life plan to buy up to $25M more in the open market. Together the buyback and the strategic holder's purchases total about $75M, roughly 20% of market cap, so the capital return is material, and the stock trades at a discount to NAV. Earnings are only modest and NAV is slipping, so the buyback is the driver. It is not an M&A deal, and the grade is strong rather than game_changer."}
{"ticker": "PAYS", "quality": "strong", "sentinel": false, "analysis": "Paysign reported Q3 2026 results on Nov 9, a fresh catalyst. Revenue was a record $30.8M, up 43%, with pharma revenue up 110%. Operating margin rose to 23.8% from 7.3%, GAAP EPS was $0.11 vs $0.04, and adjusted EBITDA rose 118%. The company raised full-year gross margin, net income, EPS and adjusted EBITDA guidance but only confirmed the revenue outlook, so this is strong rather than game_changer."}
{"ticker": "MCFT", "quality": "strong", "sentinel": false, "analysis": "MCFT reported results for the first three months of its transition period: net sales of $154.1M, up 123.4%, and up 37.4% organically excluding Marine Products. EPS was $0.50 versus $0.22 a year earlier. The Marine Products merger closed May 15, 2026, so it is a past event and not today's catalyst. Concrete numbers show strong organic growth and an earnings beat, but no guidance raise appears in the visible text, so this grades strong rather than game_changer."}
{"ticker": "CTY", "quality": "routine", "sentinel": false, "analysis": "Today's news is a press release announcing the first participant dosed in a Phase 1 trial of CITY-RBP4 for Stargardt disease, with initial data not expected until mid-2027. This is a routine early-stage clinical milestone for a pre-revenue biotech, with no efficacy data, partnership, or financial terms, so it is not a concrete catalyst that explains a significant gap-up."}
